From 14bb4dd6284be226b96697e3c2ddd365f283bcc1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jerry Zhang <jerryzh168@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 3 Apr 2026 11:01:18 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Fix torchtune ImportError after TensorCoreTiledLayout
 removal

Backport of upstream torchtune PR #2958:
  https://github.com/meta-pytorch/torchtune/pull/2958

Replace deleted TensorCoreTiledLayout with Int4PackingFormat.TILE_PACKED_TO_4D
in torchtune's Int4WeightOnlyQuantizer to fix the import error caused by the
upstream torchao change in https://github.com/pytorch/ao/pull/4153.

Adapted for the v0.6.1 tag by X. Kong <xkong@anaconda.com>:
  - At torchao 0.17.0 (the version on defaults) `TensorCoreTiledLayout` still
    exists, so #2958's own trigger has not landed yet. This backport is still
    required here for a different symbol in the same statement: torchao 0.17.0
    removed the `int4_weight_only` factory that v0.6.1 imports at module scope.
    Applying #2958 now fixes that and is forward-compatible with the
    TensorCoreTiledLayout removal #2958 actually targets.
  - v0.6.1 predates upstream's migration to the config-based torchao API and
    still calls `int4_weight_only` rather than `Int4WeightOnlyConfig`. That
    intermediate rename is folded in here; the resulting call is identical to
    the one #2958 lands.
  - v0.6.1 guards the TensorCoreTiledLayout import in a try/except that falls
    back to the torchao <=0.6 spelling (TensorCoreTiledLayoutType). Upstream had
    already dropped that fallback by #2958, so the whole block is removed rather
    than the single import line. Nothing else references the symbol.

Note: `Int4WeightOnlyQuantizer.__init__` still accepts `inner_k_tiles`, but the
TILE_PACKED_TO_4D path in torchao 0.17.0 hardcodes it to 8 (see
torchao/quantization/quantize_/workflows/int4/int4_tile_packed_to_4d_tensor.py),
so a non-default value is silently ignored. That is upstream's behaviour as of
#2958 and is left as-is deliberately; the default (8) is unchanged from v0.6.1.

Co-authored-by: X. Kong <xkong@anaconda.com>
---
diff --git a/torchtune/training/quantization.py b/torchtune/training/quantization.py
index aa8f450..42c2478 100644
--- a/torchtune/training/quantization.py
+++ b/torchtune/training/quantization.py
@@ -11,18 +11,12 @@ from torch import nn
 from torchtune.modules.peft.lora import LoRALinear, QATLoRALinear
 
 
-try:
-    # torchao 0.7+
-    from torchao.dtypes import TensorCoreTiledLayout
-except ImportError:
-    # torchao 0.6 and before
-    from torchao.dtypes import TensorCoreTiledLayoutType as TensorCoreTiledLayout
-
 from torchao.quantization import (
-    int4_weight_only,
+    Int4WeightOnlyConfig,
     Int8DynamicActivationIntxWeightConfig,
     quantize_,
 )
+from torchao.quantization.quantize_.workflows import Int4PackingFormat
 from torchao.quantization.granularity import PerGroup
 
 try:
@@ -115,8 +109,10 @@ class Int4WeightOnlyQuantizer:
         self.inner_k_tiles = inner_k_tiles
 
     def quantize(self, model):
-        layout_type = TensorCoreTiledLayout(self.inner_k_tiles)
-        quantize_fn = int4_weight_only(self.groupsize, layout_type)
+        quantize_fn = Int4WeightOnlyConfig(
+            group_size=self.groupsize,
+            int4_packing_format=Int4PackingFormat.TILE_PACKED_TO_4D,
+        )
         quantize_(model, quantize_fn)
         return model
 
